IO-02: range-check clock-time and step options

OptionsHandler stored START_TIME, END_TIME, REPORT_START_TIME and the
WET/DRY/REPORT/RULE_STEP options as parse_time_seconds() returned them, with
no check: nan and inf (read by from_chars), 1e30, and negative steps all
reached the run. A NaN start or a huge end time made the run go on past its
end date with datetime::decodeDate() converting NaN or 1e25 to int, and a
negative report step was written to the report and output as it was.

The time-of-day options must now lie between 0:00:00 and 24:00:00 (ERROR
213) and the steps must be positive (RULE_STEP non-negative) and below
2^31 s, since the output and report writers convert the report step to int
(ERROR 211). A rejected value is not stored, so the open-failure report does
not print it. This matches the patched legacy reader.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply IO-02_swmm600.patch

